# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# Shift means CAPITAL.  X11 puts the character a keypress TYPED in the
# event's text -- the key itself is the folded keysym that shortcuts
# match on, and the fold loses the case Shift put there.  An editor
# that types from the key writes lowercase whatever the hands did; the
# scripts never saw it because they passed capitals ready-made.  This
# one holds Shift the way hands do: lowercase key, shift held.
wait 14
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/caps.txt
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Documents
wait 4
menu-pick Editor
wait 90
expect-title Edit
click 60 8
wait 6
menu-pick Open…
wait 30
expect-title Open
click 400 200
wait 4
click 675 413
wait 40
expect-no-title Open
click-window Edit
wait 4
note Shift held for the H, released for the i
key h shift
wait 4
key i
wait 4
key s ctrl
wait 20
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/caps.txt Hix
click-window Edit
wait 4
key Escape
wait 30
quit
